                <pb facs="0571" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/839: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-28T13:00:00+02:00">April 28, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 28—11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. The Department may consider conveying informally to the new Greek Minister
                    before his presentation the fact that I have spoken to the Hellenic Foreign
                    Minister of the unfortunate impression which the executions would create in the
                    United States and that their accomplishment would cast a shadow on the usually
                    friendly reception of a new Greek Envoy and cause personal reversions [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">aversions?</hi>] to the President and to him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
